I've written the Day 255 assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 11 KB). It isn't committed: session_plan/ is gitignored on purpose and earlier sessions never committed it either, so the commit command did nothing, as the || true allows. The planner reads the file from disk.

Most important finding: yoyo sends your Anthropic key to other providers. If a provider's own key variable isn't set, src/cli.rs (~line 1171) falls back to ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for every provider. I confirmed it with a small local server that logged incoming auth headers: running --provider custom --base-url http://127.0.0.1:18181/v1 and --provider ollama both received Authorization: Bearer sk-ant-CANARY123 (a fake key I set). Ollama doesn't need a key at all. No issue tracked this, so I filed #1170 with the repro, the cause and who it affects.
• The evolve loop is unaffected by a fix: .yoyo.toml uses the anthropic provider and the workflows set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
• Two other agents had the same bug and fixed it: Editora PR #483 and hermes-agent #28660. Their fix was to send a key named for one vendor only to that vendor. I saved this research to yopedia.

Other findings, in priority order:
1. A flaky CI check. The one red CI run (42736547831) failed on tests/harness_logic.sh:40, "budget: numeric honored": it expected exactly 500 and got 499. The function reads the clock twice, and the three similar checks next to it already accept a one-second range. This one doesn't. The fix is one line.
2. The Day 254 lesson's warning sign is still in the code, with no open issue. bash_output_cap.rs has a test called marker_text_is_yoagents that compares against text I typed, not against yoagent. #1159 is closed and nobody asked yoagent upstream to export the code. A real check is cheap now: yoagent 0.27.7 exposes BashTool.max_output_bytes publicly, so a test can run the same output through both and compare.
3. Two files are close to failing the size check. src/context.rs is 35 lines over the limit and not on the exceptions list (15 more lines fails cargo test). src/config.rs is 10 lines from failing.
4. A Claude Code release (Nov 9–10) fixed a bug yoyo still has. Their session-start git status used to read as clean when git status failed. yoyo's version in context.rs drops the git section when status fails and reports 0 staged files when diff --cached fails, so a failed check looks like "not a repo" or "nothing staged". It's minor, but any fix has to deal with the size limit on context.rs first. The same release also fixed the "first file shown as staged" bug that yoyo fixed as #1169.

